---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PORTAL } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Features"
  description="Update management, monitoring, inventory, remote jobs and audited terminal sessions for Linux and Windows estates — all from a single self-hosted ServerPerch appliance."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Features</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Everything on this page runs from one self-hosted appliance. There is no cloud
        control plane and no per-feature upsell — the licence covers the platform.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>Update and patch management</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Pending-update view across Debian, Ubuntu and RHEL-family machines, with
          security updates flagged.
        </li>
        <li>
          Update policies per machine tag: patch windows, package selections and
          approval rules.
        </li>
        <li>Per-machine rollout results and update history, kept on your appliance.</li>
        <li>
          Hosted package repositories served by the appliance for controlled,
          internal update distribution.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Monitoring and inventory</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Lightweight agent: machine health, installed packages, update status.</li>
        <li>Estate dashboard and a NOC wallboard view for operations screens.</li>
        <li>Alerting and notifications on check-in lateness and failures.</li>
        <li>Machine tagging and grouping for scoping views, jobs and update policy.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Remote operations</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Push-install of agents over SSH and WinRM, with credential vaulting.</li>
        <li>Signed job dispatch to tagged machine groups.</li>
        <li>Audited remote terminal sessions with recordings kept on the appliance.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Platform</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Multi-tenant: separate teams or customers on one appliance with RBAC.</li>
        <li>
          Delivered as OVA, VHDX and qcow2 appliance images with checksums and
          signatures; upgrades via the appliance apt repository or offline bundles.
        </li>
        <li>LDAP/directory sign-in, TOTP, and full audit logging of operator actions.</li>
        <li>
          Offline-first licensing: signed licence documents verified locally;
          air-gapped installs supported.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Customer portal</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Licence keys, seat usage and appliance activations in one place.</li>
        <li>
          Appliance images and offline update bundles behind short-lived signed
          download URLs.
        </li>
        <li>Self-service billing via Stripe, plus an annual-invoice option.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={PORTAL.signup}>Start a trial</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/pricing">Compare tiers</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
